## opentide detection repository

This repository uses [opentide](https://pypi.org/project/opentide/): spec-driven development for agentic detection engineering.

### Commands

```bash
opentide validate
opentide generate
{deploy}
```

### Layout

- Threat vectors: `objects/threats/`
- Objectives: `objects/objectives/`
- Rules: `objects/rules/`

### Running opentide

- Run `opentide --json <command>`. stdout is one JSON document; `opentide --json commands` lists every command, option and an example.
- Branch on the exit code, then on `failure.code`: `0` success; `1` failure (`issues_found`, `command_failed`); `2` usage error (`usage_*`, with `failure.suggestion`) or a check that could not run (`no_tenant_reached`, `needs_human_decision`); `3` partial `share`.
- Each finding (`report.issues` from `validate`, `findings` from `lint`) has `code`, `path`, `line`, `column`, `end_column` (1-based, end exclusive), `help` and `fix`. Apply `fix.edits` (replace `[column, end_column)` on `line` with `replacement`); `safe: true` edits are typo fixes. Otherwise run `opentide explain <code>`.
- Follow `next_actions` (`{command, reason}`).
- opentide never prompts you: a command that needs input exits `2` with `usage_needs_input` and names the flags to pass.

### Workflow

1. Search: `opentide --json info rules`, `opentide --json info coverage --technique T1059`.
2. Draft from `.opentide/templates/`.
3. Validate until clean: `opentide --json validate --file <file>`, apply each `fix`, repeat until `ok` is `true`. Then `opentide --json lint`.
4. Preview: `opentide --json deploy --dry-run --strategy PREVIEW --all`.

People review and merge changes, and run real deployments. Do not deploy without `--dry-run` unless asked.

### Agent skills

Project skills live under `.claude/skills/`. Start with `opentide-detection-rule` for validate/generate/deploy guidance.

Run `opentide setup mcp` to connect Claude Code to the MCP server (`opentide mcp start`). Its `validation_report` and `explain` tools return the same findings and pages.
